---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CallActions from "../components/CallActions.astro";
import LoopFigure from "../components/LoopFigure.astro";
import yardulumIcon from "../assets/yardulum-icon.png";
import { PITCH } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="YardUluv, a sales tool for landscapers"
  description="YardUluv is a sales tool we’re building for Northeast Ohio landscapers, to turn a model of your customer’s yard into an itemized estimate from your own price list."
>
  <section id="hero" class="hero container" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="kicker">
        <Image
          src={yardulumIcon}
          alt="YardUluv"
          width={28}
          height={28}
          densities={[1, 2, 3]}
          loading="eager"
        />
        <span class="kicker-name" aria-hidden="true">
          YardUluv
        </span>
        <span class="chip">In development</span>
      </p>
      <h1 id="home-title">
        <span class="beat">Their yard.</span>
        <span class="beat">Your design.</span>
        <span class="beat">Your prices.</span>
        <span class="beat">Closed at the table.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">{PITCH}</p>
      <CallActions />
      <p class="byline">
        Charles Russella is building it in Kent,&nbsp;Ohio. He ran his own
        landscaping and <span class="nobr">leaf-removal</span> business.
      </p>
    </div>
    <LoopFigure />
  </section>
  <div class="container home-rest">
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="quote-heading">
      <h2 id="quote-heading">Where a quote goes wrong</h2>
      <p>
        A quote written in the truck can get the big items right and still miss
        the small ones.
      </p>
      <ul class="stories">
        <li>
          <h3>Short on mulch</h3>
          <p>
            Eyeball a bed at two yards and it takes three. Measure it, and
            324&nbsp;sq&nbsp;ft at 3&nbsp;inches is 3&nbsp;cubic yards.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>
            <span class="nobr">Haul-off</span> left off
          </h3>
          <p>
            The old sod has to go somewhere. Leave it off the quote and the crew
            hauls it for free.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The slope nobody saw</h3>
          <p>
            A yard can look flat from the driveway and still fall toward the
            street. On the model, the slope shows before anyone prices the
            grading.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We’re building YardUluv so <span class="nobr">haul-off</span>, grading
        and the rest are items you pick from your own price list, priced the
        same way on every job.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="club-heading">
      <h2 id="club-heading">Ask about the Founders Club</h2>
      <p>
        Every landscaping company that takes part before YardUluv goes on sale
        to everyone joins the Founders Club and keeps founder pricing for life,
        locked for as long as they stay members. Members get setup at their
        shop and sales training in person from Charles. In return, he asks for
        about 30&nbsp;minutes every two weeks to hear what works and what
        doesn’t.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/founders-club/">
        How the Founders Club works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="call-heading">
      <h2 id="call-heading">Call or text Charles</h2>
      <p>
        He’ll show you the property model in person and tell you where the rest
        stands. If he misses your call, he’ll call you back.
      </p>
      <CallActions />
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.12fr);
    column-gap: var(--s12);
    align-items: start;
    padding-top: var(--s10);
  }
  .kicker {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--s3);
  }
  .kicker img {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .kicker-name {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wordmark);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    margin-top: var(--s6);
    font-size: var(--text-hero);
  }
  .hero h1 .beat {
    display: block;
  }
  .hero .lead {
    margin-top: var(--s5);
  }
  .byline {
    margin-top: var(--s4);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  /* CallActions renders .actions, so reach into it with :global. */
  .hero :global(.actions) {
    margin-top: var(--s6);
  }
  .stories {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--s6) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--s8);
  }
  .stories p {
    margin-top: var(--s2) !important;
  }
  /* Two-column hero, 761-940 px: when Call and Text stack, they share the column width. */
  @media (max-width: 940px) {
    .hero :global(.actions > a) {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .stories {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s5);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      padding-top: var(--s4);
      row-gap: var(--s10);
    }
    .hero h1 {
      margin-top: var(--s4);
      font-size: var(--text-hero-phone);
    }
    .hero .lead {
      margin-top: var(--s4);
      font-size: var(--text-base);
    }
    .byline {
      margin-top: var(--s3);
    }
    .hero :global(.actions) {
      margin-top: var(--s5);
    }
  }
</style>
